WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.450
Netflix lets you revel in the good, the bad,
and the downright weird, all from the comfort

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.450
of your living room.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:11.200
It's a great place to binge watch your favorite
shows — but it's also a vast repository

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.290
of fantastic movies...if you know how to find
them.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:18.840
Wading through Netflix's recommendations can
be a daunting task, so we rounded up some

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.680
of the best hidden gems on Netflix for your
viewing pleasure.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.460
Turbo Kid

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.510
What happens when you roll every post-apocalyptic
trope into one movie, mix in absurd violence

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.550
straight from Quentin Tarantino's dreams,
and then add superheroes?

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.050
Probably something like Turbo Kid, a movie
that plays like Mad Max if the production

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.380
crew could only afford bicycles.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.579
Stay with us here.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:47.050
It's got wastelands, a water war, robots,
Soylent Green jokes, and an evil Michael Ironside

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:51.120
— which, everyone knows, is the best kind
of Michael Ironside.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.480
Remember this?

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.480
“Alright.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.379
We’re gonna do it the scanner way.

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:00.289
I’m gonna suck your brain dry.”

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:03.309
Imagine that, but with an eyepatch and less
hair.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:08.890
In the distant future of 1997, a loner kid
survives one day at a time in a wasteland,

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.359
scavenging junk to trade for water.

00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:15.240
To pass the time, he reads the adventures
of Turbo Rider, a superhero with a blaster

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.389
cannon on his arm.

00:01:16.389 --> 00:01:20.869
But when he gets on the wrong side of the
local warlord, he has to become the hero himself

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:22.310
to save his new friend.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:26.189
Don't expect any deep insights into human
nature with Turbo Kid.

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:30.669
Just enjoy it for what it is: a goofy romp
through the imagination of someone who probably

00:01:30.669 --> 00:01:34.770
grew up wearing out the scanlines on their
RoboCop LaserDisc.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.100
I Don't Feel at Home in This World Anymore

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:42.459
Call him Frodo all you want, but Elijah Wood
is working hard to reinvent his image as an

00:01:42.459 --> 00:01:44.630
actor, and we can totally respect that.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:50.799
From his mannequin-obsessed killer in 2012's
Maniac to his dirty cop con man in 2016's

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:53.869
The Trust, Wood is clearly capable of branching
out.

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:58.529
In I Don't Feel at Home in This World Anymore,
Wood plays a geeky loner who teams up with

00:01:58.529 --> 00:02:01.859
a woman in his neighborhood to find the people
who robbed her house.

00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:03.450
Don't let the title bog you down.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:08.000
It's a black comedy in the vein of the Coen
brothers' Fargo and Burn After Reading, a

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.409
subtle, escalating thriller about two everyday
people thrust over their heads into a world

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:15.790
of crime where anything can — and does — go
wrong.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.570
I Don't Feel at Home in This World Anymore
is moody, occasionally hilarious, and surprisingly

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.849
poignant.

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:24.820
“I’m not letting you shoot anyone.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.900
Anyone else.”

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:31.680
Makkhi

00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:36.330
If you've never watched much Bollywood, it
may be hard to tell if Makkhi is making fun

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.370
of those films or comfortably nestled at the
heart of it all.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:44.129
The absurdity feels intentionally cranked
to 11, but then again, there's also a distinct

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:49.260
possibility that a song-and-dance number followed
by a Rocky training montage for a reincarnated

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.219
fly is completely normal.

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:53.840
Either way, it's totally worth your time to
watch.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.970
Here's the premise, and it's a doozy: A fly
born from the soul of a dead man goes on a

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.860
revenge rampage against the guy who killed
him.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.420
It's John Wick crossed with A Bug's Life crossed
with…uhhh...La-La-Land?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.260
Maybe?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.890
There's a trippy Ant-Man vibe to the visuals
and explosive action sequences, all tied into

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:16.390
a deathmatch between a man and, well, a housefly.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:21.060
As far as hidden gems go, this one's like
stumbling across a dead unicorn in the woods.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.220
It's majestic.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.520
And you just don't know what the hell to do
with it.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.520
Harlock: Space Pirate

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:31.630
From the outset, you can look at Harlock:
Space Pirate and expect a rocket-fueled amount

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.630
of fun.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:36.519
After all, a movie with the gumption to call
itself exactly what it is in the title isn't

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:41.099
about to bore you with over-long, tedious
insights into the internal struggles of being

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:42.099
a space pirate.

00:03:42.099 --> 00:03:47.170
No, you're getting spaceships, laser bombs,
robot suits, and — in case you missed it

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.379
the first time — space pirates.

00:03:49.379 --> 00:03:54.379
Based on a Japanese manga, Harlock: Space
Pirate was well-received on its release in

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:59.760
2013 and even won Best International Animated
Feature at the 3D Creative Arts Awards.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.930
But the CG spectacle didn't come anywhere
close to making back its production budget

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.709
and ultimately failed to find much of an audience.

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:08.950
Does that mean you should steer clear of Harlock?

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:09.950
Not even close.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:14.219
If the geek pleasure centers of your brain
light up at the thought of a well-made, beautifully

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:19.620
animated sci-fi adventure, you'll definitely
get a kick out of Harlock: Space Pirate.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.410
The Beaver

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:25.520
Mel Gibson had a rough couple years in the
mid-aughts, and although he's now got another

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.110
Oscar-winning film under his belt, his return
to Hollywood didn't come without a few false

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:31.110
starts.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:36.290
In 2011, he starred in Jodie Foster's film
The Beaver as Walter Black, the CEO of a toy

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.509
company who has a nervous breakdown, loses
his family, and tries to hang himself from

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:42.090
a hotel shower curtain.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.530
On the edge of death, Black snaps completely
— and allows his life to be taken over by

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.919
a beaver puppet.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.260
“I love you.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:57.280
I’m the only one that really, really loves
you.”

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:01.250
It's technically a comedy, but dark doesn't
come close to describing the humor.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:06.020
This is blacker than a coal mine after a cave-in,
an intimate portrait of depression and mental

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:10.550
illness that flows so seamlessly from Gibson's
acting that you can't help but believe he's

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.060
channeling his own personal experiences.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.650
With incredible supporting performances from
Jodie Foster, Anton Yelchin, and Jennifer

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.229
Lawrence, The Beaver is definitely a hidden
gem worth watching, if only once.

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:26.270
Although afterward you may need to watch something
a little more light-hearted.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.680
Like The Human Centipede.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.220
Thanks for watching!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.210
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.569
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

